  "prefLabel": "Agr 705.05 Economic Viability",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-21",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 705.05 Economic Viability.\n\n(a) The committee shall evaluate the economic viability and supporting services to maintain agricultural production.\n\n(b) Availability of wholesale and retail markets for commercial products and supplies and services required for agricultural production shall qualify the application for 5 points.\n\n(c) Information relevant to demonstrating availability of these markets shall be furnished in the following for:\n\n(1) A list of where and how the agricultural products produced on the land are marketed; and\n\n(2) A list of the major sources of supplies, such as seeds, fertilizers, feed, and equipment, such as purchase and repair, necessary to maintain the agricultural production.\n\n(d) Concentration of farm and agricultural activity shall qualify the application for 5 points.\n\n(e) The maximum points awarded for this section shall be 10.\n\nSource. #1601, eff 7-1-80; ss by # 2237, eff 1-1-83; ss by #2887, eff 10-22-84; ss by #4098, eff 7-22-86, EXPIRED: 7-22-92\n\nNew. #7463, eff 3-21-01, EXPIRED: 3-21-09\n\nNew. #13910, eff 3-21-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Agr 700)",
